# Benchmark artifacts. Written into the repo root by `bench/run.ts`, so they land
# next to the working tree rather than in a scratch directory.
#
# Enumerated one by one until this change, which is the defect: the list named the
# three artifacts that existed when it was written and nothing since, so every
# artifact added later -- the recall curve, the gap attribution, the failure
# census, the TR classes, the skip record, and all three ablation report pairs --
# was committable. A measurement is not source, and committing one makes a
# figure that must be re-derivable look like a tracked fact; it also means a
# single `git add -A` after a local run silently ships the operator's numbers.
#
# A glob covers the whole family and, more importantly, covers the next artifact
# too -- which is what an enumeration cannot do, and what went wrong here.
benchmark-*
# Probe scratch. `tools/run-program.py --keep` writes improvised programs here so a
# probe survives the session that wrote it instead of living in scrollback.
#
# Ignored for the same reason as the benchmark artifacts, and for one more: a probe
# is evidence *for* a conclusion, not the conclusion, so a tracked probe would make
# a discarded line of investigation look like a supported claim. The directory is
# named rather than globbed because probes are always written here and nowhere else.
probe/

